 after  watching free guy many many times and  the atom project last night sean levy is  going to do an absolutely incredible job  directing deadpool 3. he's just recently  worked with ryan reynolds on these last  two movies so the chemistry is obviously  really really good there and it looks  like they've just decided to keep the  ball rolling right into deadpool 3. now  if you watched free guy and i hope you  did because it's amazing there was  actually quite a bit of marvel in the  movie specifically towards the end we  had captain america shield we had a hulk  hand we had a lightsaber which isn't  marvel but star wars and chris evans  even made a tiny little cameo sean levy  has expressed before how much of a huge  marvel fan he is and specifically a huge  deadpool fan so no doubt over the past  few years while they were doing these  movies free guy and the atom project  ryan reynolds and sean talked about  deadpool and what they could make  together and yesterday ryan reynolds  even took to twitter to react to the  news that sean levy would be directing  deadpool 3. in a twitter post yesterday  he tweeted the third film in my sean  levi trilogy will be a tad more stabby  and then he put a picture that had the  three characters he's played with sean  levy so far on the right is guy from  free guy in the middle is adam from the  atom project and of course we all know  who is on the left deadpool so this  tweet even further confirms that sean  levi is going to be directing deadpool 3  and ryan reynolds is very excited about  it now we also do have a little bit more  news about the direction the script is  going it appears that the first draft of  the script is done about a year ago it  was announced that the maulanos sisters  were going to be writing the script for  deadpool 3 and they did along with ryan  reynolds of course but the hollywood  reporter stated that the molino sisters  finished the first draft of the film  however now rhett reese and paul wernick  are now writing the second draft of the  script and doing the screenplay and this  is also fantastic news because they  wrote the scripts for the first two  deadpool films so if we have a lot of  people out there worried that now that  deadpool is over at disney and not over  at fox if you're worried that he's going  to be changing a lot do not be worried  about that we have the same writers plus  ryan reynolds said he wanted to be a lot  more hands-on for deadpool 3 as far as  the script is concerned and direction is  concerned and now we have an amazing  director who has great chemistry with  ryan reynolds already and is a huge  deadpool fan you do not have to worry  about deadpool changing it sounds like  they're definitely sticking true to the  character and i trust ryan reynolds i  think even if they got a completely new  team marvel studios in disney made them  get an entire new staff ryan reynolds  would still stick true to who deadpool  was and let's be honest deadpool in the  mcu is kind of just ryan reynolds we  kind of associate them as one person  let's be honest so even if it was just  ryan reynolds coming back i'm sure it  would still be a great deadpool film but  we have an amazing cast and crew right  now and right now there are kind of two  important questions that we really need  to ask and we should note that ryan  reynolds did say that he would be making  a deadpool 3 announcement soon now he  didn't really make this announcement the  other day he came out and said that he  wanted sean levy to direct deadpool 3  and then yesterday the hollywood  reporter came out and they reported on  it but he didn't say anything and marvel  studios didn't say anything so perhaps  we'll be getting an official deadpool 3  announcement from ryan reynolds and  marvel studios relatively soon in an  interview not too long ago marvel  studios president kevin feige did say  that they did have a release date down  for deadpool 3 already so perhaps that  release date is going to be announced  relatively soon now as far as those two  important questions are concerned the  first one that we have to ask is will  deadpool be rated are still even though  it's in the mcu and over at disney well  first things first let's not forget what  former ceo bob iger said about deadpool  in the mcu now he said deadpool can  remain rated r he didn't say deadpool  could be rated r or we'll see about it  he said it's going to remain rated r  which is a great sign now he's no longer  the ceo bob chapeck is but you would  like to assume that they kind of have  the same thought process after all  deadpool and deadpool 2 are two of the  biggest grossing rated r movies of all  time record-breaking rated r movies and  fans love them it would be unwise to  change deadpool to a pg-13 movie but  this is actually coming right around the  time that all of the netflix marvel  shows are about to be released on disney  plus and these are definitely more  mature now disney plus is making some  adjustments to their parental controls  on the streaming service and this is  also a very good sign that deadpool can  remain rated r and not to mention marvel  is getting a little bit more risky we  did in fact have our first sex scene in  the eternals it wasn't much but hey it's  there and that just shows you that  really what marvel is going for is good  filmmaking and i don't think you can do  a deadpool movie if it's not rated r and  i think marvel and disney knows this but  the second biggest question we of course  have is will deadpool actually make his  mcu appearance before deadpool 3 and i  think the answer to this of course is  yes i think deadpool is going to be  introduced to the mcu in multiverse of  madness with all of these crazy  different rumors going around about all  of these different cameos that could  happen in doctor strange 2. i think one  that makes the most sense is deadpool  deadpool can enter the mcu this way  going from the fox universe to the mcu 